    "title": "Ukraine Begins Mass Production of Interceptor Drones - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Davis ,\n3 hours ago Ukraine has moved from prototypes to mass production of low-cost interceptor drones.\nBuilt by volunteer startups, these mobile interceptors aim to blunt faster, higher-flying Russian suicide drones.\nFederico Borsari, defense analyst at the Center for European Policy Analysis, says the drones are a crucial part of counter-UAS efforts.\nTOPSHOT – President of Ukraine Volodymyr Zelenskyy (Photo by Genya SAVILOV / AFP via Getty Images) “Cheap interceptor drones have become so important, and so quickly, that we can consider them a cornerstone of modern counter-unmanned aerial systems. They realign the cost and scale equation of air defense,” Borsari said.\nAndrii Lavrenovych, strategic council member at General Cherry, says Ukraine will expand co-production with U.S. and European firms in 2026.\nDefense experts say rapid mass production and planned co‑production with U.S. and European firms could bolster Ukraine’s air defense and improve NATO interoperability.\nThis story was reported by content partner Modern Newsstand LLC.",
